# Graph Alignment Notebook

This notebook inspects the new graph builders against the paper-aligned contract. Treat `docs/social-attention.pdf` as the authority; historical code and the upstream submodule are audit references only.

## Synthetic Flat Keypoint Graph

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.12"}
from pathlib import Path
import sys

import numpy as np

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/social_nav").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from social_nav.graphs import build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph

keypoints = np.arange(3 * 3 * 12 * 2, dtype=np.float32).reshape(3, 3, 12, 2)
graph = build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph(keypoints)

print("variant:", graph.variant)
print("nodes:", graph.nodes.shape)
print("edges:", graph.edge_features.shape)
print("frame 0 present edges:", len(graph.edges_present[0]))
print("frame 1 present edges:", len(graph.edges_present[1]))
```

