## Real MABe Window Graph

```python {"interpreter":"/home/splion/Desktop/personal/interpreting-social-navigation/.venv/bin/python3.12"}
from pathlib import Path
import sys

repo_root = next(path for path in [Path.cwd(), *Path.cwd().parents] if (path / "src/social_nav").exists())
sys.path.insert(0, str(repo_root / "src"))

from social_nav.data import MabeDataset, MabeWindowDataset, WindowSpec
from social_nav.graphs import build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph, build_mouse_level_graph

dataset = MabeDataset.from_file(repo_root / "data/MaBe/mouse_triplet_train.npy")
sequence = dataset.sequences[dataset.sequence_ids[0]]
window = MabeWindowDataset(
    [sequence],
    WindowSpec(length=20, observation_length=8, prediction_length=12, stride=20),
    max_windows=1,
).first()

flat_graph = build_flat_sparse_keypoint_graph(window.keypoints)
mouse_graph = build_mouse_level_graph(window.keypoints)

print("sequence:", window.sequence_id)
print("window:", window.keypoints.shape)
print("flat nodes/edges:", flat_graph.nodes.shape, flat_graph.edge_features.shape)
print("mouse nodes/edges:", mouse_graph.nodes.shape, mouse_graph.edge_features.shape)
```

## Audit Notes

- Flat graph: 36 nodes, one per mouse keypoint. Temporal self-edges start at frame 1; frame 0 has only spatial edges present.
- Sparse spatial policy: directed cross-mouse keypoint edges only. Same-mouse anatomical edges are intentionally left to geometry/structural losses until the paper contract requires them in the interaction graph.
- Mouse-level graph: 3 centroid nodes with directed inter-mouse spatial edges. This is the seam for the future hierarchical model.
- Historical `scripts/st_graph.py` should be audited as reference behavior, not treated as the target contract.
